@startuml generated-drivers-two-ladders
' ============================================================================
' The 2x2 experiment that identified the cross-type hop as THE mechanism behind
' eight sloped generated drivers.  MEASURED 2026-07-29, RLIMIT_STACK bisection.
'   RED   #C62828 sloped — a live defect
'   GREEN #2E7D32 flat
'   TEAL  #00695C control
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4

title <b>Two ladders, nine generated drivers</b>\nthe cross-type hop is the mechanism — confirmed 9 for 9

rectangle "**LADDER A — ALTERNATING CATEGORIES**\n`nested_list`: ``Proc::CastList(Arc<List>)`` then ``List::ListLit(Vec<Proc>)``\nthe hop is crossed at EVERY level" as A #FFEBEE {
  card tableA #FFFFFF [
    |= driver |= debug B/level |= release B/level |= |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_cmp"" |<#EF9A9A> **""10,592.4""** |<#EF9A9A> **""335.3""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_debug"" |<#EF9A9A> **""10,544.2""** |<#EF9A9A> **""463.8""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_eq"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 6,144.0""** |<#EF9A9A> **""175.7""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_normalize"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 6,144.0""** |<#EF9A9A> **""176.7""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_match_pattern"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 6,138.0""** |<#EF9A9A> **""174.7""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_subst"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 6,134.0""** |<#EF9A9A> **""174.7""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_hash"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 1,216.8""** |<#EF9A9A> **""206.8""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF9A9A> ""ast_semantic_hash"" |<#EF9A9A> **"" 1,214.7""** |<#EF9A9A> **""206.8""** |<#EF9A9A> |
    |<#EF5350> ""ast_drop"" |<#EF5350> **""   254.0""** |<#EF5350> **"" 96.4""** |<#EF5350> //the one pre-existing subject — reproduced to the byte// |
    |<#A5D6A7> ""ast_display"" |<#A5D6A7> **""     0.0""** |<#A5D6A7> **""    0""** |<#A5D6A7> ★ FLAT — its driver DOES follow the hop |
    |<#66BB6A> ""ast_clone"" |<#66BB6A> **""     2.0""** |<#66BB6A> **""    0""** |<#66BB6A> ★ FLAT — it does not traverse at all |
    |<#80CBC4> ""build_twins"" (control) |<#80CBC4> **""     1.0""** |<#80CBC4> **""    0""** |<#80CBC4> |
  ]
}

rectangle "**LADDER B — PURE SINGLE CATEGORY**\n`nested_add`: ``Proc::Add(Arc<Proc>, Arc<Proc>)``\nno hop exists to cross" as B #E8F5E9 {
  card tableB #FFFFFF [
    |<#A5D6A7> **every one of the nine: <latex>\approx 0</latex> B/level** |
    |<#A5D6A7> ""ast_cmp"" ""ast_debug"" ""ast_eq"" ""ast_normalize"" |
    |<#A5D6A7> ""ast_match_pattern"" ""ast_subst"" ""ast_hash"" |
    |<#A5D6A7> ""ast_semantic_hash"" ""ast_display"" ""ast_drop"" |
    |<#80CBC4> ""build_twins_add"" (control)  <latex>\approx 0</latex> |
  ]
}

A -[#455A64,thickness=3]down-> B : the ONLY difference is the SHAPE walked

note right of A #FFEBEE
  ★★ **Eight sloped drivers were a live defect class in `macros/src/gen/`** (since
  repaired at the classifier — SS-G4), not a
  documentation gap: depth-independence is these modules' entire purpose.
  Figures are **debug / release** B/level, ladder <latex>16 \rightarrow 4{,}096</latex>,
  bisected at 4 KiB resolution on the child's MAIN thread.
end note

note right of B #E8F5E9
  The controls are flat on **both** ladders, so every slope in ladder A is the
  **driver's own** and not the builder's or the harness's.
  <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> The generated work stacks are typed **per category** and do not
  follow an edge that leaves their own type.
end note

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#EF9A9A>| sloped on the alternating ladder — the defect |
  |<#EF5350>| the one pre-existing subject (`ast_drop`) |
  |<#A5D6A7>| flat |
  |<#66BB6A>| flat by REPRESENTATION (<latex>\mathtt{Arc::clone}</latex>), not by a driver |
  |<#80CBC4>| control — runs no driver |
endlegend

@enduml
